WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.921 --> 00:00:06.548
This is Valery.

00:00:10.969 --> 00:00:13.471
She was 5 years old when 
she received chemotherapy.

00:00:47.338 --> 00:00:49.507
Valery would receive 
chemotherapy treatments here

00:00:49.507 --> 00:00:51.676
at the Clinica Medical Duarte

00:00:51.676 --> 00:00:54.554
in the small border city of 
Cúcuta, in Colombia. 

00:00:55.805 --> 00:00:59.100
On Jan. 23, 2020, doctors at the clinic

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:02.979
gave Valery a dose of Methotrexate, 
a drug used to treat cancer. 

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:07.108
Less than 24 hours later, 
she was back in the hospital. 

00:01:08.026 --> 00:01:09.319
Days later, she was dead.  

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:12.864
The drug Valery was given, Methotrexate, 

00:01:12.864 --> 00:01:17.660
was made by Naprod Life Sciences, a manufacturer headquartered in India

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:21.039
a country that supplies 20% of the world’s generic drugs. 

00:01:21.706 --> 00:01:24.501
But instead of being sterile, the medicine was contaminated 

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:26.795
with bacteria and had 
become dangerous. 

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:31.424
In a months-long investigation, we learned this wasn’t an isolated incident. 

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:34.719
Naprod’s medicines have been 
linked to dire quality issues 

00:01:34.719 --> 00:01:37.097
with almost zero consequences. 

00:01:38.181 --> 00:01:41.267
This is the story of a drugmaker with 
a dangerous track record 

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:44.145
and how it keeps selling medicine, leaving families and doctors

00:01:44.145 --> 00:01:45.939
to suffer the consequences.

00:01:57.867 --> 00:02:00.161
Methotrexate is a drug 
used to treat leukemia 

00:02:00.161 --> 00:02:02.831
and other cancers, and has 
been around for decades.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:07.335
When given as an injection, the conditions in which the drug is made

00:02:07.335 --> 00:02:08.920
are always supposed to be sterile.

00:02:09.712 --> 00:02:12.048
If the raw ingredients 
aren’t tested adequately, 

00:02:12.048 --> 00:02:13.967
if a production line 
isn’t cleaned properly, 

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:16.136
if the water isn’t filtered thoroughly, 

00:02:16.136 --> 00:02:19.305
the life-saving medicine could 
become potentially lethal.

00:02:21.724 --> 00:02:24.519
Naprod Life Sciences plays a crucial, 
if sometimes unnoticed, 

00:02:24.519 --> 00:02:26.771
role in the world’s drug supply chain. 

00:02:29.524 --> 00:02:31.901
None of its medicines are 
for sale in the US. 

00:02:31.901 --> 00:02:35.822
Instead, it mostly sells directly to suppliers in low-income countries. 

00:02:36.114 --> 00:02:38.491
Batches of the cancer drug methotrexate,

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:42.620
made here in 2018 and 2019 
were sent to clinics in Colombia. 

00:02:43.079 --> 00:02:46.291
Later, Colombian drug regulators confirmed that a dangerous bacteria 

00:02:46.291 --> 00:02:47.458
was found in the drug. 

00:02:49.043 --> 00:02:52.213
Doctors suspected more than 
100 patients had suffered reactions

00:02:52.213 --> 00:02:54.424
linked to the contaminated medicine. 

00:02:54.424 --> 00:02:57.468
A total of 4 kids died.
 And the drug was later recalled.  

00:03:02.765 --> 00:03:06.561
My colleague Priyanka Pulla looked 
into Naprod’s operations in India. 

00:03:06.936 --> 00:03:10.023
This is a plant that makes many 
low cost cancer generics

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:14.319
for big brand names such as Intas, 
Dr Reddy’s and Abbott.

00:03:14.694 --> 00:03:18.198
Former employees of Naprod 
whom we spoke to told us 

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:21.784
that the quality control in this company was not up to the mark, 

00:03:21.784 --> 00:03:24.037
and was neglected greatly.

00:03:24.954 --> 00:03:28.708
The former quality control employee spoke to us on condition of anonymity.

00:03:29.417 --> 00:03:31.878
He was asked to hurry 
through quality tests.

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:08.289
Indian regulators have frequently failed to detect and clamp down 

00:04:08.289 --> 00:04:10.291
on really dangerous quality issues.

00:04:45.743 --> 00:04:50.290
State governments are very eager to attract the pharmaceutical industry

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:52.917
and to get them to set up their manufacturing plants 

00:04:52.917 --> 00:04:56.296
because it helps them 
generate revenue and jobs.

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:59.924
 And the state regulators are directly under these state governments.

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:05.805
These state regulators are not very well staffed. They are underfunded. 

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:07.390
 if you put these two things together,

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:10.810
 it's a very dangerous cocktail 
because this means that

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:15.273
India's huge manufacturing industry doesn't get as much oversight 

00:05:15.273 --> 00:05:16.858
as it needs.

00:05:17.358 --> 00:05:20.320
This wasn’t the first time quality issues were found at Naprod. 

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:24.073
In India, 3 separate batches of its cancer drugs failed quality tests

00:05:24.073 --> 00:05:25.867
in 2017 and 2018. 

00:05:25.867 --> 00:05:29.829
In Ethiopia, researchers tested multiple samples of its chemo drug 

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:32.332
and found only half of the
 stated active ingredient.

00:05:32.332 --> 00:05:36.336
Yet the company has not faced any serious consequences from regulators,

00:05:36.336 --> 00:05:38.713
the big pharmaceutical companies buying Naprod’s products, 

00:05:38.713 --> 00:05:41.090
or public health warnings from the World Health Organization. 

00:05:41.591 --> 00:05:43.760
Naprod declined to 
comment on Valery's case 

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:47.305
or other cases in Colombia, citing ongoing legal proceedings. 

00:05:48.431 --> 00:05:51.434
The company said it has responded appropriately to quality concerns 

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:54.354
raised by regulators and makes 
high quality products.

00:06:25.802 --> 00:06:28.096
So who is to blame for Valery’s death? 

00:06:28.096 --> 00:06:29.722
And how can people 
in low-income countries 

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:31.265
ensure their drugs are safe?

00:06:33.309 --> 00:06:36.145
Despite its track record, Naprod continued selling medicines

00:06:36.145 --> 00:06:41.067
around the world, cashing in on growing markets for generic cancer drugs. 

00:06:41.818 --> 00:06:44.070
And Valery’s case is 
stuck in the labyrinth 

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:46.072
of Colombian government bureaucracy. 

00:06:46.948 --> 00:06:50.576
The attorney general’s office received Valery's autopsy report four years ago.

00:06:51.035 --> 00:06:53.579
It has listed her cause of death 
as “under study.” 

00:06:54.872 --> 00:06:59.377
In the years that have passed, there have been few signs of progress in the probe. 

00:06:59.377 --> 00:07:02.880
In recent months, the attorney general's office has started interviewing families

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:04.090
and others involved.

00:07:05.925 --> 00:07:10.721
But 2,500 miles away, a researcher in the US is trying to perfect 

00:07:10.721 --> 00:07:14.767
a test to help detect bad quality drugs before they reach patients. 

00:07:15.935 --> 00:07:19.730
The market for chemotherapy 
products is increasing

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:24.569
and it's increasing in locations where often the regulatory agencies 

00:07:24.569 --> 00:07:27.947
are under-resourced, 
particularly for analysis 

00:07:27.947 --> 00:07:31.200
of highly toxic chemotherapy products. 

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:33.786
And so it's a very risky 
situation right now.

00:07:34.787 --> 00:07:37.665
The paper test her team 
developed is a field lab kit

00:07:37.665 --> 00:07:42.336
 run on a sample of medicine, testing for the amount of active ingredient. 

00:07:43.629 --> 00:07:47.717
It costs as little as $2 and can be done easily by a nurse using a cellphone.  

00:07:48.301 --> 00:07:54.223
These are a field screening device that you can use to check a medicine quickly 

00:07:54.223 --> 00:07:57.852
and see if it looks good 
or if it looks suspicious.

00:08:00.438 --> 00:08:02.773
Nearly four years after Valery's death, 

00:08:02.773 --> 00:08:06.319
Naprod continues to sell its drugs to customers around the world.

